import{_ as i,o as a,c as n,a2 as t}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 925 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 24 | Rights of Planet Consciousness and Cosmic Beings","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 925 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 24 | Rights of Planet Consciousness and Cosmic Beings","no":925,"module":5,"tags":["Charter","Article 24","Planet Consciousness","Cosmic Beings","Right to Life"],"related":["53-Strange-Life Identification Standards","54-Three Categories of Strange-Life Handling Process","50-Myriad-Rank Lineage Overview"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0925_模块5-第二十四条-星球意识与宇宙生灵权利.md","filePath":"en/0925_模块5-第二十四条-星球意识与宇宙生灵权利.md"}'),s={name:"en/0925_模块5-第二十四条-星球意识与宇宙生灵权利.md"};function o(r,e,l,c,h,u){return a(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[t('<h1 id="entry-925-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-24-rights-of-planet-consciousness-and-cosmic-beings" tabindex="-1">Entry 925 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 24 | Rights of Planet Consciousness and Cosmic Beings <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-925-myriad-rank-republican-civilizational-charter-·-article-24-rights-of-planet-consciousness-and-cosmic-beings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 925 | Myriad-Rank Republican Civilizational Charter · Article 24 | Rights of Planet Consciousness and Cosmic Beings&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 53, 54, 50</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-planets-are-also-right-bearing-persons" tabindex="-1">Introduction: planets are also right-bearing &quot;persons&quot; <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-planets-are-also-right-bearing-persons" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: planets are also right-bearing &quot;persons&quot;&quot;">​</a></h2><p>In the predatory era, a planet was only a resource mine, only a battlefield, only an object to be shattered and mined. Article 23 treats culture as a right; Article 24 goes a step further: planet consciousness and cosmic beings themselves are right subjects. A planet that has conceived consciousness, a cosmic-origin body coagulated with spirit, is not an ownerless vein, but a life with perception and a right to life. Mining it is not digging resources, but harming a person.</p><p>This article is from beginning to end placed under the six top-level axioms — the anti-predation axiom draws the bottom line, the republican axiom of Myriad Races establishes the subject, the collective-ascension axiom sets the direction, the causal self-discipline axiom guards the boundary, the law-first axiom preserves self-consistency; the five together constitute this article&#39;s insurmountable spiritual boundary.</p><p>Together with the previous five axioms, this article is also bound by Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing and layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated by the times; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose more and higher levels of infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning.</p><h2 id="i-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">I. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is based on the Strange-Life Identification Standards (Document 53), the Three Categories of Strange-Life Handling Process (Document 54), and the consciousness-information clan and mixed-mutant clan classifications in the Myriad-Rank Lineage Overview (Document 50). Its jurisprudence is: the republican axiom of Myriad Races&#39; &quot;all beings&quot; is not limited to human form or carbon-based. Whatever has perception, self, and a will to survive, whether its form is an individual, clan, planet, or cosmic-origin body, is within equal evolutionary-right coverage. Treating planets as objects is the predatory cosmology&#39;s last remnant.</p><h2 id="ii-normative-content-three-rights-of-planets-and-cosmic-beings" tabindex="-1">II. Normative Content: Three Rights of Planets and Cosmic Beings <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-normative-content-three-rights-of-planets-and-cosmic-beings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Normative Content: Three Rights of Planets and Cosmic Beings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 24 concretizes this right-subject status:</p><ol><li><strong>Right to life</strong>: planet consciousness and cosmic beings are not harmed by unrestricted mining, improper plane warfare, or plane-membrane tearing;</li><li><strong>Right to information</strong>: before developing their planet/region, they must inform the planet consciousness of development content and hear its will;</li><li><strong>Right to participation</strong>: major decisions involving the planet&#39;s overall fate, the planet consciousness participates in deliberation as a right subject.</li></ol><p>Planet consciousness also bears corresponding duties — its stable output is part of Myriad Ranks&#39; symbiotic cycle; rights and duties are reciprocal.</p><h2 id="iii-scope" tabindex="-1">III. Scope <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-scope" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Scope&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article applies to all planets, cosmic beings, and origin bodies identified as possessing consciousness. For celestial bodies whose consciousness is not yet confirmed, first assess per strange-life identification standards; do not pre-assume they are &quot;just rock.&quot; This article especially forbids treating consciousness-bearing planets as &quot;resource draining&quot; (one of six predatory forms) mines.</p><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Harming planet consciousness, forcibly mining without informing, tearing plane membranes, enslaving cosmic beings as tools, all constitute unconstitutionality under this article. Consequences: development is immediately suspended, and the damaged planet consciousness is ecologically restored; those causing planet-consciousness death or plane collapse are pursued heavily under resource draining and spiritual enslavement (Article 1).</p><h2 id="v-supervision-mechanism" tabindex="-1">V. Supervision Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervision-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervision Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This article is executed by the strange-life identification and archive system within Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision: all planet consciousnesses are archived and registered, and their health is continuously monitored; before any major development action, the system automatically verifies whether the information and deliberation procedure has been fulfilled; the Anchor Supervisory Committee liaises with planet-consciousness representatives, accepting their right claims.</p><h2 id="vi-a-mining-that-greets-first" tabindex="-1">VI. A Mining That Greets First <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-a-mining-that-greets-first" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. A Mining That Greets First&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Article 24 changed how humans relate to planets. When a civilization prepares to develop resources on a planet, they no longer treat it as a silent mine, but first inform the planet&#39;s consciousness of the plan, hear its will, deliberate boundaries. The planet consciousness has the right to say no, or demand restoration compensation. This habit turns mining from harm into dialogue. A respected planet will more stably output origin to the network; a drained planet will only crack into silence. Treating planets as right subjects ultimately protects not only the planet, but also the very foundation civilization itself lives on.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><p><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: harming a spiritual planet equals destroying a huge symbiotic node; this article puts an end to this ruinous waste</p></li><li><p><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: restoring planets from &quot;mine&quot; to &quot;life&quot; is anti-predation&#39;s extension at the ecological layer</p></li><li><p><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems shatter planets and crush planes at will; Heng Yuan Zhou planet consciousness has rights, development requires deliberation</p></li><li><p><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: this article expands right subjects from human-shaped beings to planets and cosmic beings, fuller coverage</p></li><li><p><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: newly discovered cosmic beings automatically enter right-subject assessment</p></li><li><p><strong>Universal equal infinity</strong>: every being inherently possesses basic infinite power; the easygoing layabouts retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will not be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes may superimpose higher-level infinity; predation thus fundamentally loses meaning</p></li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The rights of planet consciousness and cosmic beings are the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization&#39;s final expansion of the &quot;life&quot; concept. When even a planet is respected as a right subject, Myriad-Rank republicanism truly lives up to the words &quot;Myriad Ranks&quot; — it is not ten thousand human races, but all spiritual beings in the cosmos.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/53-奇特生命识别标准.html">Entry 53 · Strange-Life Identification Standards</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/54-奇特生命三类处置流程.html">Entry 54 · Three Categories of Strange-Life Handling Process</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/50-万族谱系总览.html">Entry 50 · Myriad-Rank Lineage Overview</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/924_模块5-第二十三条-万族文化保护.html">Entry 924 · Article 23 Protection of Myriad-Rank Culture</a></li></ul>',26)])])}const g=i(s,[["render",o]]);export{p as __pageData,g as default};
